sing the commutative law, we can swap the order of the words \"strawberry\" and \"orange.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The juice is orange or strawberry.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $(M∧N)∧(N∨N).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40635742-9288-5d2d-bfdc-3674acf9908b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572688 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the associative and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(M∧N)∧(N∨N) & ≡(M∧N)∧N \\\\  & ≡M∧(N∧N) \\\\  & ≡M∧N.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128616" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $(A∨B)∨A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5aad22c2-f4b5-5b1b-92ab-159f5eea4c65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572693 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the commutative, associative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∨B)∨A & ≡(B∨A)∨A \\\\  & ≡B∨(A∨A) \\\\  & ≡B∨A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128618" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $(A∧A)∧(B∧A).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6f4a26a2-aaa2-5db2-88b4-6bb08153b831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572696 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the associative, commutative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧A)∧(B∧A) & ≡A∧(B∧A) \\\\  & ≡A∧(A∧B) \\\\  & ≡(A∧A)∧B \\\\  & ≡A∧B.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83008" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the following sentence: \"The watch is a wristwatch, or it is a pocket watch or it is a wristwatch.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7fde2761-bb61-54c2-b335-1663af74408b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572699 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"it is a pocket watch or it is a wristwatch\" with the phrase \"it is a wristwatch or it is a pocket watch.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The watch is a wristwatch, or it is a wristwatch or it is a pocket watch.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"The watch is a wristwatch or it is a wristwatch, or it is a pocket watch.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"The watch is a wristwatch or it is a wristwatch\" to just \"The watch is a wristwatch.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The watch is a wristwatch, or it is a pocket watch.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"The watch is a wristwatch or a pocket watch.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the sentence \"The house is pretty, or it is pretty or white.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9609c9d7-0f30-5ae1-9971-3c66a1bfd653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572705 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the phrase \"it is pretty or white\" as the equivalent phrase \"it is pretty or it is white.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The house is pretty, or it is pretty or it is white.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"The house is pretty or it is pretty, or it is white.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"the house is pretty or it is pretty\" to just \"the house is pretty.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The house is pretty, or it is white.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"The house is pretty or white.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83006" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the following sentence: \"The day is rainy and it is cold, and the day is rainy.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ac648f3a-f305-5539-9491-09df3a7946e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572707 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the commutative law, we can replace the phrase \"The day is rainy and it is cold\" with the phrase \"The day is cold and it is rainy.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The day is cold and it is rainy, and the day is rainy.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"The day is cold, and it is rainy and the day is rainy.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"it is rainy and the day is rainy\" to just \"it is rainy.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The day is cold, and it is rainy.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely:\n\n\"The day is cold and rainy.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83016" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $P∨(Q∨P).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b8b24239-40f1-5136-9956-57abae0c726e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572712 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the commutative, associative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∨(Q∨P) & ≡P∨(P∨Q) \\\\  & ≡(P∨P)∨Q \\\\  & ≡P∨Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $(A∨A)∧(A∧B).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d4c8e41b-9e14-5786-91ae-524e6c4c4e4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572717 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the associative and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∨A)∧(A∧B) & ≡A∧(A∧B) \\\\  & ≡(A∧A)∧B \\\\  & ≡A∧B.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89251" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the sentence \"The dress is red and elegant, and it is elegant.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d9600c9e-6c82-5b6e-b3f2-54ca64b173d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572718 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the phrase \"The dress is red and elegant\" as the equivalent phrase \"The dress is red and the dress is elegant.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The dress is red and the dress is elegant, and it is elegant.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"The dress is red, and the dress is elegant and it is elegant.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"the dress is elegant and it is elegant\" to just \"the dress is elegant.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"The dress is red, and the dress is elegant.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"The dress is red and elegant.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186572597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $(Q∧P)∧Q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd1f6b88-5ede-50c3-bec3-63756a7c54a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186572729 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the commutative, associative, and idempotent laws, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Q∧P)∧Q & ≡(P∧Q)∧Q \\\\  & ≡P∧(Q∧Q) \\\\  & ≡P∧Q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
